---
description: Lift the brain-state detector from src/tools/info/buildBrainState/ to src/service/buildBrainState/, switch to the fixed `brain` MCP key, dispatch to the brainBackends registry for identity, and surface `BrainState.backend` on every branch.
intent: >
  Move the existing brain-state detector to the service layer so both
  aide_info (boot probe) and aide_brain (runtime tool) can consume it
  without crossing horizontal-isolation boundaries; replace the legacy
  `obsidian` MCP key lookup with the fixed `brain` key; dispatch the
  resolved entry to `brainBackends.resolveBackend` and store
  `driver.id` on `BrainState.backend` for `ok`; collapse the new
  wired-but-unrecognized case to `no-mcp-entry` with `backend: null`;
  preserve every existing edge-case branch and its tests; delete the
  old location once the lift is complete.
---

## Project Structure

The tree below shows `src/service/buildBrainState/` after this plan executes.
Every file inside this scope directory is listed; cross-cutting edits to
files outside this directory (`src/tools/info/index.ts`,
`src/tools/info/index.test.ts`, and the deletion of
`src/tools/info/buildBrainState/`) are declared as explicit steps below
but are not part of this module's folder tree.

```
src/service/buildBrainState/
├── .aide                ← [existing] intent spec for this orchestrator
├── plan.aide            ← [this file] implementation plan
├── index.ts             ← [new — lifted from src/tools/info/buildBrainState/index.ts] orchestrator: buildBrainState(root: string) => Promise<BrainState>
└── index.test.ts        ← [new — lifted from src/tools/info/buildBrainState/index.test.ts] co-located vitest covering ENOENT, malformed JSON, missing brain key, malformed args, empty-args, non-string last arg, empty-string vault path (cold install), Windows-shape args, hints surfaced, ok-with-stat-dir, stat-rejects, stat-resolves-to-file, AND the new wired-but-unrecognized branch (resolveBackend → null)
```

The orchestrator has no helper subfolders. It composes three external
helpers — `detectFramework` (sibling service), `resolveBrainHints`
(sibling service), and `resolveBackend` (sibling service registry) —
plus `node:fs/promises` primitives. None of those become local helpers
under this module; they each live in their own module per horizontal
isolation.

## Prerequisites

Two upstream contracts must already be in place before this plan runs.
Both have already shipped (see `## Decisions` below for the audit).

### 1. `src/types/index.ts` — `BrainState.backend` field

Must already export `BrainState` with the new `backend: string | null`
field defined and JSDoc-documented per `src/tools/brain/plan.aide`
step 1c. This plan **reads** the type and **populates** the field —
it never re-defines or extends `BrainState`. Confirmed in place at
plan-write time (`src/types/index.ts` lines 385–411).

### 2. `src/service/brainBackends/index.ts` — registry contract

Must already export:
- `default function resolveBackend(entry: McpServerEntry): BackendDriver | null`
  — returns the matched driver or `null` when no matcher fires; never
  throws; never falls back to a default backend.
- (Available for downstream consumers, not used by this plan)
  `function getDriverById(id: string): BackendDriver | null`.
- Re-exports of `BackendDriver` and `McpServerEntry` from
  `@/types/index.js`.

This plan dispatches the wired entry shape to `resolveBackend` exactly
once per `buildBrainState` call. The internal matcher table, the
Obsidian launcher predicate, and the instruction template are all owned
by the registry; this plan never inspects `command`/`args` shapes
itself. Confirmed in place at plan-write time
(`src/service/brainBackends/index.ts`).

## Plan

### 1. Create the lifted orchestrator at `src/service/buildBrainState/index.ts`

Read: `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`, `coding-playbook/architecture/folder-structure`, `coding-playbook/services/error-handling`

- [x] 1a. Create `src/service/buildBrainState/index.ts` with a default
      export `async function buildBrainState(root: string): Promise<BrainState>`.
      Single-positional `(root: string)` signature — single-input
      object rule applies to two-or-more arguments; one argument stays
      positional per the spec.
- [x] 1b. Imports:
        - `readFile`, `stat` from `node:fs/promises`
        - `join` from `node:path`
        - default `detectFramework` from `@/service/install/detectFramework/index.js`
        - default `resolveBrainHints` from `@/service/install/resolveBrainHints/index.js`
        - default `resolveBackend` from `@/service/brainBackends/index.js`
        - types `BrainHint`, `BrainState`, `McpServerEntry` from `@/types/index.js`
- [x] 1c. Pipeline (declarative, sequential — no Promise.all between
      `detectFramework` and `resolveBrainHints` because the existing
      detector ran them sequentially and that ordering is preserved
      verbatim by the lift; reordering or parallelizing is out of
      scope for the lift). The orchestrator runs:
        1. Resolve framework config: `await detectFramework(root)` →
           join `frameworkConfig.mcpConfigPath` to `root` for the
           absolute MCP config path.
        2. Resolve hints: `await resolveBrainHints(root)`. Populated
           unconditionally so every returned `BrainState` carries the
           same hints array.
        3. Read the MCP config file. Wrap `readFile(..., "utf-8")` in
           try/catch. ANY read failure (ENOENT or otherwise) collapses
           to `no-mcp-entry` with `vaultPath: null`, `backend: null`,
           `hints`. Never rethrow.
        4. Parse JSON. Wrap `JSON.parse(raw)` in try/catch. Any parse
           failure collapses to the same `no-mcp-entry` shape as
           step 3. Never rethrow.
        5. Look up the **fixed `"brain"` key** in `mcpServers`. The
           existence check uses `"brain" in (servers as object)` —
           NOT `"obsidian"`. The legacy `obsidian` fallback is
           **forbidden** per the spec's undesired outcome (legacy
           migration is the install service's job). If `mcpServers`
           is missing, not an object, or has no `brain` key, return
           the same `no-mcp-entry` shape.
        6. Extract `args` from the brain entry. If `args` is missing,
           not an array, or empty → `no-mcp-entry`,
           `vaultPath: null`, `backend: null`, `hints`. The vault
           path extraction rule is unchanged from the existing
           detector: `args[args.length - 1]` (last positional element,
           platform-agnostic — covers POSIX
           `["@bitbonsai/mcpvault", <path>]` and Windows
           `["/c", "npx", "@bitbonsai/mcpvault", <path>]`).
        7. Validate the candidate path. If `args[args.length - 1]` is
           not a string → `no-mcp-entry`. If it is the empty
           string → `invalid-path` with `vaultPath: ""`,
           `backend: null` (deliberate cold-install state from
           `provisionBrain`).
        8. **NEW BRANCH — registry dispatch.** Build a typed
           `entry: McpServerEntry` from the brain entry's `command`
           and `args` (defensively narrow `command` to a string;
           `args` is already proven to be a string-tail array at
           this point). Call `resolveBackend(entry)`. If the registry
           returns `null` (wired-but-unrecognized backend), return
           `no-mcp-entry` with `vaultPath: null`, `backend: null`,
           `hints`. Per the spec's strategy this collapses to the
           same `no-mcp-entry` shape as "never wired at all" — same
           remediation, no new vocabulary.
        9. Stat the candidate vault path. Wrap `stat(candidatePath)`
           in try/catch. If it rejects OR the result's
           `isDirectory()` is false → `invalid-path` with the
           configured `candidatePath`, `backend: null`, `hints`.
       10. Happy path: return `{ status: "ok", vaultPath: candidatePath, hints, backend: driver.id }`
           where `driver` is the non-null result from step 8. The
           `backend` field is the registry-resolved driver's `id`
           string — NEVER hardcoded to `"obsidian"`.
- [x] 1d. Discriminant invariants enforced by the branch returns:
        - `status: "ok"` ⇒ `vaultPath: string` AND `backend: string` (the resolved driver id).
        - `status: "no-mcp-entry"` ⇒ `vaultPath: null` AND `backend: null`.
        - `status: "invalid-path"` ⇒ `vaultPath: string` (configured path or `""`) AND `backend: null`.
        Never return `backend: null` on `ok` and never return a
        non-null `backend` on `no-mcp-entry`/`invalid-path`. These
        rules are JSDoc-documented on the type (already done in
        `src/types/index.ts`); enforce them via the branch return
        literals here.
- [x] 1e. Multi-line JSDoc on the default export. The narrative
      mirrors the existing detector's JSDoc but updated for the new
      contract: lookup uses the fixed `"brain"` key (no `obsidian`
      fallback; legacy migration is the install service's job),
      backend identity comes from `resolveBackend` (never from the
      key name), the wired-but-unrecognized case collapses to
      `no-mcp-entry`, and every branch returns a structured value
      including the new `backend` discriminant. Each branch in the
      function body gets a `// Step N — …` comment naming which
      spec outcome it satisfies. Do not duplicate the type
      definition into JSDoc.
- [x] 1f. **Forbidden patterns the implementor must NOT introduce**
      (each is called out by the spec's bad examples):
        - No `if ("obsidian" in servers)` fallback when `brain` is
          absent.
        - No hardcoded `backend: "obsidian"` literal anywhere — the
          id always comes from `driver.id`.
        - No inspecting `command`/`args` shapes inside this module
          to derive backend identity. Pass the entry to
          `resolveBackend`; trust the result.
        - No storing the `BackendDriver` object on `BrainState.backend` —
          store only `driver.id` (a plain string).
        - No introducing a new status (`unsupported-backend` etc.)
          for the wired-but-unrecognized case.
        - No throwing on any branch.

